# PER-PART TRACK MUTES: in MIX (and TRACKS) a BLACK key 1-6 mutes that track IN THE PART (a bit of the part, saved with the project);
# a white key 1-6 only selects the track. Stopped: at once; playing: it waits for the bar's end (pending, blinking). There is no
# temporary mute and no clear-by-holding any more. Each part has its own mask.
wait 300
tap SAVE
wait 100
tapkey w4
wait 200
expect nev 0
listen
seed 0 1 4 1
seed 0 2 4 0
seed 1 1 2 0
setbars 0 2
page 3
wait 100
expect page 3
expect pmask 0
# stopped: at once, toasts A: <track> MUTED / ON
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect pmask 1
said MUTED
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect pmask 0
said ON
tapkey b1
wait 100
expect pmask 2
expect pmaskB 0
# playing: the toggle waits for the bar's end
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 1
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect pmpend 1
expect pmask 2
said BAR END
# toggled again before the bar's end: cancelled (nothing pending)
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect pmpend 0
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect pmpend 1
wait 3400
expect pmpend 0
expect pmask 3
expect part 0
# HOME + black selects the track and mutes nothing; a white key only selects (no temp mute, no clear)
press HOME
tapkey b2
release HOME
wait 100
expect track 2
expect pmask 3
tapkey w3
wait 100
expect track 3
expect pmask 3
tapkey b0
wait 3600
expect pmask 2
# holding a black key is still one toggle, and clears nothing
expect eventsA2 4
key b1 down 90
wait 1200
key b1 up
wait 3600
expect eventsA2 4
expect pmask 0
tapkey b1
wait 3600
expect pmask 2
# another part has its own mask: B is asked for, at the bar's end the song is in B, whose mask is 0
press ARP
tapkey w1
release ARP
wait 4700
expect part 1
expect pmask 0
expect pmaskA 2
# pending while stopping: applied
tapkey b3
wait 100
expect pmpend 8
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
expect pmpend 0
expect pmaskB 8
# NEW PART = EMPTY does not touch masks; the masks are saved with the project and come back
wait 92000
expect dirty 0
reboot
wait 300
expect pmaskA 2
expect pmaskB 8
expect pmaskC 0
